Z||000000||Lisa 86 2m4||01-21-2001||07:19 PM||||Just an off question... I was reading an auto mag the other day and Bosch had an add in for thier oxygen sensor with the statement to change it at every oil change.<BR>How true is that?<BR>THanks for quelching my curiosity!<BR>Lisa||||reg||1
Z||000001||87GTZ34||01-21-2001||07:23 PM||||Well that does a couple of things...  First off it will improve bosch's earnings and therefore stock price with a increase of steady revenue; and secondly, it will ensure that your O2 sensor will rarely fail.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Edit:  I forgot to add that, if that is true, they don't have a quality product... The EPA has set goals for auto manufacturers that no emmisions critical parts should need to be replaced within 100k mile intervals (including plugs).<p>[This message has been edited by 87GTZ34 (edited 01-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||01-21-2001||07:31 PM||||They do get slow, but every oil change? I don't think so. Maybe 25k miles.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Lisa 86 2m4||01-21-2001||08:36 PM||||I was thinking it had to be for their profit margins, but I worried just a little bit because as far as I can remember, I have never replaced mine. Phew!||||reg||1
Z||000004||MrPBody||01-21-2001||08:43 PM||||My wife's Jeep Cherokee has a service timer that turns-on a warning light every 90K miles (I think) to remind us to change the oxygen sensor.  The timer self-destructs so we have to replace that, too.  Would it work better to change the sensor more often?  I dunno.  Probably.<P>So there's a range:  somewhere between every oil change and 90,000 miles.  I'm guessing that Bosch doesn't advocate changing your oil at 90,000-mile intervals.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by MrPBody (edited 01-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||88formula||01-21-2001||10:04 PM||||About every 30k is the norm.||||reg||1
Z||000006||ka4nkf||01-21-2001||10:59 PM||||If it aint broke,don't fix it. if the oxygen sensor fails, your check engine light will come on and set a code in your computer.||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||01-21-2001||11:36 PM||||I'd have to see the ad. Information I have from Bosch and others indicate the O2 sensors will last years unless they are contaminated.<P>||||reg||1
